      "hints": [
        "Use $S_\\infty = \\frac{5a}{1 - (-1/4)}$ for the GP.",
        "Use $S_8 = \\frac{8}{2}(2a + 7(-4))$ for the AP.",
        "Equate $4a = 8a - 112$ and solve for $a$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Calculate the sum to infinity of the geometric progression with first term $5a$ and common ratio $r = -\\frac{1}{4}$:\n$$S_\\infty = \\frac{5a}{1 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)} = \\frac{5a}{\\frac{5}{4}} = 4a$$",
        "Calculate the sum of the first $8$ terms of the arithmetic progression with first term $a$ and common difference $d = -4$:\n$$S_8 = \\frac{8}{2}\\left(2a + (8 - 1)(-4)\\right) = 4(2a - 28) = 8a - 112$$",
        "Equate the two sum expressions as given by the problem:\n$$4a = 8a - 112$$",
        "Solve the linear equation for $a$:\n$$4a = 112 \\implies a = 28$$"
      ],
